{"seconds": 33.9, "exit": 0, "final": "So after Qc6+ Qd7 Qxa8+ Qd8, White is simply up a rook. The material gain is decisive.\n\n**Best move: Qc6+**\n\n**Main line:** Qc6+ Ke7 Qxa8 (or Qd7 Qxa8+)\n\n**Motif: fork** (the queen checks the king and attacks the rook)\n\n**Coaching explanation:**\nWhen your opponent's king is uncastled and stuck in the center, look for checks that simultaneously threaten loose pieces. Here, Qc6+ forces Black's king to move, then you capture the undefended rook on a8. The queen forks the king and rook\u2014a simple tactic that wins material decisively. Always scan checks first and see what else they threaten.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qc6+\", \"line\": [\"Qc6+\", \"Ke7\", \"Qxa8\", \"Qd8\", \"Qa7\", \"Kd6\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "square": "e8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "square": "b7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "move": "Qc6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "move": "Qb5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "move": "Qe4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/p1p2ppp/2Q5/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 1 10", "move": "Ke7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2q1bnr/p1p1kppp/